    {
      "id": "8f9f4553-8b20-46de-a150-a3d72184fddf",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Overview & setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -720,
        -784
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 620,
        "height": 2152,
        "content": "# Extract structured data from any webpage using Apify and AI\n# 📥 [Open full documentation on Notion](https://automatisation.notion.site/Course-Extract-structured-data-from-any-webpage-using-Apify-and-AI-3a03d6550fd98114843fe82b3ab7ed8e)\n\n## How it works\nSend a POST request to the webhook with either a direct `target_url`, or a `subject` + `website_domain` pair to search for. The workflow resolves the page, scrapes it with [Apify](https://apify.com/?fpr=firas)'s Website Content Crawler (clean Markdown, no browser to maintain, optional login cookies), then an AI agent extracts exactly the fields listed in `target_data` and the result is returned to the caller as JSON. Every failure path answers the caller with an explicit status code instead of timing out.\n\nCanvas map, left to right:\n1. Receive & validate the request\n2. Resolve the target URL (direct or search)\n3. Scrape the page with Apify\n4. Extract with AI & respond\nBottom lane: every early-exit response (400 validation, 404 not found, 502 upstream, 200 with success:false).\n\n## Setup\n1. Create an Apify account and copy your API token from Console > Integrations.\n2. Create an \"Apify API\" credential in n8n: type **Header Auth**, Name = `Authorization`, Value = `Bearer YOUR_APIFY_TOKEN`.\n3. Select that credential on **Search Page with Apify** and **Scrape Page with Apify**.\n4. Select your OpenAI credential on the **OpenAI Model** sub-node.\n5. Adjust the defaults in the **Configuration** node if needed, then activate the workflow.\n\n## Requirements\nAn Apify account (pay-as-you-go, first $5 free) and an OpenAI API key. No self-hosted browser, no proxy setup, no Docker required.\n\n## Example request body\n```\n{\n  \"target_url\": \"https://example.com/pricing\",\n  \"target_data\": [\n    { \"name\": \"plan_name\", \"description\": \"Name of the cheapest paid plan\" },\n    { \"name\": \"price\", \"description\": \"Monthly price of that plan\" }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Customization\n- `target_data`: array of `{ \"name\", \"description\" }` objects describing exactly what to extract, any number of fields.\n- `cookies`: optional array of browser-exported cookies to scrape pages behind a login.\n- Tune `crawler_type`, `max_crawl_pages`, `min_content_length` and `openai_model` in **Configuration**.\n\n---\nNeed help customizing?\nContact me for consulting and support : [Linkedin](https://www.linkedin.com/in/doctor-firass/)\n\n# MY NEW YOUTUBE CHANNEL\n👉 [Subscribe to my new YouTube channel](https://www.youtube.com/@DrFiras_AI). Here I'll share videos and Shorts with practical tutorials and FREE templates for n8n.\n\n[![The AI Doctor](https://www.dr-firas.com/the-ai-doctor.png)](https://www.youtube.com/@DrFiras_AI)"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c2c34cf9-270c-47ba-bc57-697dd3d6804c",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Step 1 Receive & validate",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -80,
        -160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1160,
        "height": 340,
        "content": "## 1. Receive & validate the request\nThe webhook accepts the POST payload, **Configuration** centralises every adjustable setting, then the body is normalised into flat fields and `target_data` is checked. Without it the caller gets a 400 straight away."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "2c1ffa9c-3ffe-42b5-81f4-48b3a715802b",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Step 2 Resolve URL",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1104,
        -400
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1080,
        "height": 580,
        "content": "## 2. Resolve the target URL\nTwo ways in: a `target_url` is used as is (top branch), otherwise the domain is searched with Apify's Google Search Scraper and the first organic result is taken (bottom branch). Both branches converge on the scraper."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "7a082b01-e9f0-44c4-aec6-b3422a52360d",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Step 3 Scrape",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2224,
        -160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 800,
        "height": 340,
        "content": "## 3. Scrape the page with Apify\nNo Selenium, no Docker, no proxy whitelist: the Website Content Crawler returns clean Markdown, with optional cookies for logged-in pages. The content is then normalised and checked against `min_content_length`."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "f6570557-7d45-4925-8f5a-794ec86c38ef",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Step 4 Extract & respond",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        3072,
        -160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 640,
        "height": 700,
        "content": "## 4. Extract with AI & respond\nThe Structured Output Parser schema is built dynamically from the `target_data` the caller sent, so any number of fields works, not a hardcoded list. The agent returns only what it found on the page and the JSON is sent back to the caller."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "80278392-2349-4fd8-a263-55fec923fb66",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Early exits",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1104,
        560
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
